= The <span style="color: [+ linke_color +];">**Bewegungslinke**</span>

In the last two years, a new caucus in our party has been gaining traction. It is the Movement Left, a group opposing both the post-communist pragmatism and Wagenknecht's conservative populism to form a new form of radical intersectional socialism. While the Bewegungslinke's rise in popularity is undeniable, there are many in the party that would rather see it fail.
  
- @embrace_bwl: Embrace the BWL and its intersectionalism as the only way to social equality.
- @deny_bwl: We will not become a party of blue-haired, they/them hipsters.

@embrace_bwl
on-arrival: beweli_strength += 5; oldleft_dissent += 3; wagenknecht_left_progress += 1; issue_feminism += 0.5; youth_linke += 1*(1-dissent); social_moderation -= 0.2;

We have decided to support the Movement. However, it is too soon to predict where it will go...

@deny_bwl
on-arrival: oldleft_strength += 8; beweli_strength -= 15; beweli_dissent += 15; oldleft_dissent -= 5; pragmatist_dissent -= 1; wagenknecht_left_progress -= 5; social_moderation += 3;

Asterisks and pronouns can only damage our party.
